# Line-ending policy: scripts must reach every platform as LF — bash on
# Windows (MSYS) fails on carriage returns. `text=auto` normalizes what git
# classifies as text; the explicit rules below are load-bearing regardless of
# any user's core.autocrlf.
* text=auto
*.sh text eol=lf
*.md text
# eol=lf: the plugin cache is a byte copy of a checkout — pin JSON to LF so
# an autocrlf=true clone cannot ship CRLF manifests (and so the CR guard in
# tests/check-plugin.sh stays truthful on such clones).
*.json text eol=lf
